  "summary": "San Francisco Mayor Daniel Lurie announced new privacy restrictions on the SFPD's Flock Safety ALPR network, shortening data retention from 12 months to 30 days and requiring every search to be tied to a CAD or incident number. The changes follow an internal audit that found out-of-state and federal agencies had improperly accessed the data. The ACLU of Northern California called the reforms insufficient without a warrant requirement.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "the San Francisco Police Department can access license plate reader data for 30 days after the data is captured, down from 12 months",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "an internal audit of its ALPR camera network showed it was improperly accessed by outside agencies over the past year",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "The proposal for internal supervision would do little to stop law enforcement from running searches of our locations",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    }
  ],
